---@class vercel.integrations.GetConfigurationResponseBodyCase0
---@field acceptedPoliciesInheritedFromInstallationId? string Historical parent installation from which acceptedPolicies were inherited. This is immutable provenance, not current authorization or relationship truth.
---@field canConfigureOpenTelemetry? boolean
---@field completedAt? number A timestamp that tells you when the configuration was installed successfully
---@field createdAt number A timestamp that tells you when the configuration was created
---@field customerDeleteRequestedAt? number|distilled.Null Record when the customer initited deletion, independent of whether `deleteRequestedAt` gets set.
---@field deletedAt? number|distilled.Null A timestamp that tells you when the configuration was deleted.
---@field deleteRequestedAt? number|distilled.Null A timestamp that tells you when the configuration deletion has been started for cases when the deletion needs to be settled/approved by partners, such as when marketplace invoices have been paid.
---@field disabledAt? number A timestamp that tells you when the configuration was disabled. Note: Configurations can be disabled when the associated user loses access to a team. They do not function during this time until the configuration is 'transferred', meaning the associated user is changed to one with access to the team.
---@field disabledReason? vercel.integrations.GetConfigurationResponseBodyCase0DisabledReason
---@field externalId? string An external identifier defined by the integration vendor.
---@field id string The unique identifier of the configuration
---@field installationType? vercel.integrations.GetConfigurationResponseBodyCase0InstallationType Defines the installation type. - 'external' integrations are installed via the existing integrations flow - 'marketplace' integrations are natively installed: - when accepting the TOS of a partner during the store creation process - if undefined, assume 'external'
---@field integrationId string The unique identifier of the app the configuration was created for
---@field notification vercel.integrations.GetConfigurationResponseBodyCase0Notification
---@field ownerId string The user or team ID that owns the configuration
---@field projects? vercel.integrations.GetConfigurationResponseBodyCase0ProjectsList When a configuration is limited to access certain projects, this will contain each of the project ID it is allowed to access. If it is not defined, the configuration has full access.
---@field projectSelection vercel.integrations.GetConfigurationResponseBodyCase0ProjectSelection A string representing the permission for projects. Possible values are `all` or `selected`.
---@field scopes vercel.integrations.GetConfigurationResponseBodyCase0ScopesList The resources that are allowed to be accessed by the configuration.
---@field slug string The slug of the integration the configuration is created for.
---@field source? vercel.integrations.GetConfigurationResponseBodyCase0Source Source defines where the configuration was installed from. It is used to analyze user engagement for integration installations in product metrics.
---@field status? vercel.integrations.GetConfigurationResponseBodyCase0Status The configuration status. Optional. If not defined, assume 'ready'.
---@field teamId? string|distilled.Null When the configuration was created for a team, this will show the ID of the team.
---@field type vercel.integrations.GetConfigurationResponseBodyCase0Type
---@field updatedAt number A timestamp that tells you when the configuration was updated.
---@field userId string The ID of the user that created the configuration.

